-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Jun 23 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Andreas Røsdal <andreas.rosdal@gmail.com>

- Release 1.0.14.
- Media: inline WebM playback — VP9/VP8 video and Opus/Vorbis audio —
  decoded in-tree through an optional FFmpeg libav* backend. On Linux the
  system FFmpeg is used (a runtime dependency, never bundled); the macOS
  and Windows builds vendor a minimal, LGPL-only FFmpeg carrying just those
  decoders. Other codecs, and Android, keep the external-player fallback.
- CSSOM: a real CSSRule / CSSStyleRule / CSSGroupingRule / CSSMediaRule
  object model with document.styleSheets, insertRule/deleteRule, spec
  serialization of style rules and media queries, and a CSSStyleDeclaration
  iterator.
- Images: HTMLImageElement.decode() is now spec-compliant (rejects with an
  EncodingError for undecodable or missing sources); createImageBitmap()
  accepts Blob sources and rejects undecodable ones with InvalidStateError;
  canvas drawImage() validates its source type.
- Text tracks: a working addTextTrack / textTracks (TextTrackList) /
  <track>.track model with WebVTT loading, a start-time-ordered cue list,
  and addtrack/removetrack events.
- Media probing: canPlayType() now reports accurate per-codec support so
  pages can select a playable <source>.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Jun 22 10:00:00 UTC 2026 - Andreas Røsdal <andreas.rosdal@gmail.com>

- Initial openSUSE package of Nordstjernen 1.14, a small, hand-written
  web browser written from scratch in C with a GTK 4 UI and a libcurl
  network stack.
- Built from git via the OBS scm bridge (scmsync); ai/webgpu features
  disabled, wasm disabled on 32-bit x86 (WAMR does not build there).
- Licensed under the Nordstjernen Source License v1.0 (NSL-1.0), a
  source-available, non-free license; packaged for the non-OSS area.
